# Credentials for `npm run errors` — pulls live errors into .errors/.
#
#   cp .env.errors.example .env.errors
#
# This file is gitignored. It holds a real login to a live hospital, so treat
# it the way you would treat that login: don't paste it into a chat, don't
# commit it, and use an account that only has errors:view if you can.
#
# Configure EITHER block. With both, --source picks; without it, HMS wins.

# --- Your own deployment (default) ---
# The public URL of the running app — the same one you open in a browser.
HMS_URL=https://your-app.onrender.com
HMS_EMAIL=admin@yourhospital.com
HMS_PASSWORD=
# Which hospital, in a multi-tenant deployment. Leave as 'default' unless you
# have provisioned others.
HMS_TENANT=default

# --- Sentry (optional) ---
# Settings → Auth Tokens → Create. The only scope needed is event:read.
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=sntrys_...
# SENTRY_ORG=your-org
# SENTRY_PROJECT=hms
# Self-hosted Sentry only:
# SENTRY_HOST=https://sentry.example.com
